      "receiptId": "everlasting-syllabub.html-1",
      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt in \u0027\u003Ci\u003EA New System Of Domestic Cookery\u003C/i\u003E\u0027 by \u0027A Lady\u0027 (Mrs. Maria Eliza Ketelby Rundell) (\u003Ca href=\u0022references.html#rundell-1807\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003ERundell 1807\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E);",
      "receiptText": "\u003Cb\u003EEVERLASTING SILLABUBS\u003C/b\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\nMix a quart of thick raw cream, one pound of refined sugar, a pint and a half of fine raisin wine in a deep pan; put to it the grated peel and the juice of three lemons. Beat or whisk it one way half an hour, then put it on a sieve with a bit of thin muslin laid smooth in the shallow end till next day. Put it in glasses It will keep good in a cool place ten days.\u003Cbr\u003E"
    }
